{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792549084184,"sessionID":"ses_ea3e01b08ffe25JrGjIjfiH29d","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_25ee933d76164d8a8953a8ca","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"{\n  \"option_title\": \"Exhaustive capsid–receptor complex enumeration (docking and AlphaFold-Multimer)\",\n  \"question\": \"Does exhaustive modeling of AAV capsid–receptor complexes reveal a shared interface motif, like 3-fold-axis GPI-receptor engagement, that marks which capsids transcytose the BBB?\",\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Transcytosis-competent capsids engage GPI-anchored BBB receptors at the capsid 3-fold spike with a shared anchor geometry, unlike non-cognate pairs [s_appraise].\",\n  \"compute_axis\": {\n    \"quantity\": \"capsid–receptor pose models computed per panel sweep (rigid-docking poses plus AlphaFold-Multimer seed models)\",\n    \"unit\": \"pose models\",\n    \"levels\": [144, 720, 2880]\n  },\n  \"held_fixed\": [\n    \"the 12-capsid library (AAV9, AAV2, PHP.B, PHP.eB, PHP.eC, 9P31, 9P36, VCAP-102, AAV9-X1.1, CAP-Mac, CAP-B22, AAV-BI30)\",\n    \"the 6-receptor panel (LY6A, LY6C1, ALPL, LRP6 E1E2, CA4, AAVR PKD2)\",\n    \"constructs: capsid VR-IV plus VR-VIII loops against receptor ectodomains\",\n    \"ColabFold v2.3.5 AlphaFold-Multimer-v3 settings: 5 models, up to 20 recycles, MMseqs2 MSAs [s_lrp6_gpu]\",\n    \"docking search space: VP trimer with the insertion loop as anchor\",\n    \"motif definition: contact centroid within 15 Å of the 3-fold axis, GPI anchor vector within 30° of the membrane normal\",\n    \"published phenotype labels used for scoring\",\n    \"8x NVIDIA A100 SXM 40GB instances at $1.99 per GPU-hour [s_lambda]\"\n  ],\n  \"predictions\": {\n    \"if_lever\": \"At 2,880 models the competent-minus-retained GPI-engagement gap reaches 0.50 or more, while at 144 models it stays below 0.25.\",\n    \"if_not\": \"The gap stays within 0.15 of its 144-model value at every depth; added poses change nothing because insert location already fixes the 3-fold site [s_cat].\",\n    \"decision_rule\": \"Paired comparison of the motif gap at 2,880 versus 144 models on the same 72 pairs: call if_lever if the gap rises by at least 0.25 with disjoint bootstrap 95% intervals; call if_not if it moves less than 0.15 and per-pair seed agreement kappa is at least 0.8; otherwise unsure.\",\n    \"noise_rule\": \"Five AlphaFold seeds per pair vote on motif class, pairs with kappa below 0.8 are unresolved; paired bootstrap over 72 pairs gives intervals; a fresh-seed medium rerun must reproduce the gap within 0.10.\",\n    \"expected\": \"if_not\",\n    \"expected_why\": \"Capsid insertions already sit on the 3-fold spike [s_cat] and AlphaFold-Multimer poses for these weak interfaces vary by run and version [s_appraise_unstable], so extra poses add noise rather than a converged signature.\"\n  },\n  \"compute_tested\": \"yes\",\n  \"compute_tested_why\": \"Each pose model is an independent docking or AlphaFold-Multimer job with its own seed, so the model count of 144, 720 or 2,880 is exactly what extra parallel GPUs buy.\",\n  \"scored_against\": \"Published capsid–receptor phenotype labels: PHP.B/PHP.eB–LY6A and VCAP-102–ALPL transcytosis versus AAV9 and AAV2 retention [s_ly6a][s_alpl][s_voyager_pr], plus the published PHP.eB–LY6A binding pose and contacts [s_appraise_rmsd].\",\n  \"arms\": [\n    {\"id\": \"arm_shallow\", \"what\": \"72 pairs at 2 pose models each (1 docking pose plus 1 AlphaFold seed): 144 models; first motif gap\"},\n    {\"id\": \"arm_medium\", \"what\": \"Same 72 pairs at 10 pose models each: 720 models; the intermediate snapshot\"},\n    {\"id\": \"arm_deep\", \"what\": \"Same 72 pairs at 40 pose models each (20 docking poses plus 20 AlphaFold seeds): 2,880 models\"},\n    {\"id\": \"arm_md\", \"what\": \"20 explicit-solvent MD refinements of 20 ns on top cluster representatives\"},\n    {\"id\": \"arm_anchor\", \"what\": \"Reproduction of the published PHP.eB peptide–LY6A complex and the LRP6–X1 peptide complex before library spend\"},\n    {\"id\": \"arm_controls\", \"what\": \"Negative control: a non-receptor protein run against 12 capsids at shallow depth to measure the hallucination rate\"}\n  ],\n  \"baseline\": {\n    \"what\": \"Published depth for this computation: ten AlphaFold-Multimer models per receptor competition matrix [s_appraise_rep] and two LRP6 peptide complexes with five models each [s_lrp6]; the minimal arm here is one pose model per pair.\",\n    \"value\": 10,\n    \"source_id\": \"s_appraise_rep\"\n  },\n  \"anchor\": {\n    \"what\": \"Rebuild the published PHP.eB peptide–LY6A complex and require its validated contacts and capsid fit before any library spend [s_appraise].\",\n    \"published_value\": 0.36,\n    \"tolerance\": \"capsid-fragment RMSD to PDB 7WQO at most 1.5 Å (published engineered-loop RMSD is 1.36 Å) and at least 2 of the 3 named contacts (peptide Pro5', Phe6', LY6A Ala58) within 5 Å\",\n    \"source_id\": \"s_appraise_rmsd\",\n    \"independent_code\": \"the RosettaRemodel integrative pipeline of Shay et al. 2023 [s_appraise_3fold], run apart from our ColabFold-plus-docking pipeline\"\n  },\n  \"checks\": [\n    \"Anchor first: PHP.eB–LY6A rerun must reproduce Pro5'/Phe6' and LY6A Ala58 contacts within 5 Å and capsid RMSD to 7WQO within 1.5 Å before any library spend [s_appraise_rmsd].\",\n    \"Positive controls: cognate pairs PHP.eB–LY6A, 9P31–CA4, VCAP-102–ALPL and AAV9-X1.1–LRP6 must rank in the top quartile of interface confidence [s_ly6a][s_cat][s_alpl][s_lrp6].\",\n    \"Negative control: a non-receptor protein against 12 capsids at shallow depth must not yield stable 3-fold motif calls above 20 percent.\",\n    \"AAV9 and AAV2 must show no stable LY6A pose; AAV9 is a published non-binder [s_appraise].\",\n    \"Seed stability: motif class unchanged across at least 4 of 5 seeds (kappa at least 0.8); unstable pairs marked unresolved rather than forced.\",\n    \"MD stability: refined pose interface backbone RMSD below 3 Å over 20 ns.\",\n    \"Noise floor: a fresh-seed medium rerun reproduces the motif gap within 0.10.\",\n    \"GPI geometry: receptor C-terminal attachment vector within 30° of the membrane normal in every pose counted as GPI-engaging.\"\n  ],\n  \"phases\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"p0_inputs\",\n      \"what\": \"Fetch 12 capsid and 6 receptor constructs, build the 72 pair FASTAs, run the symmetry-axis precheck that each engineered insertion lies on the 3-fold spike [s_cat_vr]\",\n      \"gate\": {\"on\": \"n_capsids_ready\", \"op\": \">=\", \"value\": 9, \"else\": \"shrink the library to ready capsids, re-derive the pair grid and re-price before any GPU spend\"}\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"p1_pilot\",\n      \"what\": \"On one 8x A100 instance: reproduce the PHP.eB–LY6A anchor, time 6 representative pair jobs, one docking job and 2 ns MD, write pilot/pilot_metrics.txt with pilot/run_pilot.py\",\n      \"stop_rule\": \"Timer 3 hours; no library spend until the anchor contacts reproduce\",\n      \"gate\": {\"on\": \"af_job_min\", \"op\": \"<=\", \"value\": 20, \"else\": \"halve af_seeds_deep to 12 per pair and re-price; stop entirely if jobs exceed 30 min\"}\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"p2_shallow\",\n      \"what\": \"Compute 2 pose models for every pair (1 docking pose plus 1 AlphaFold seed): 144 models, and the first motif gap\",\n      \"stop_rule\": \"Timer 4 hours; deliver the 144-model snapshot even if some pairs have fewer poses (mark them unresolved)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"p3_deep\",\n      \"what\": \"Deepen each pair to 40 pose models (20 docking poses plus 20 AlphaFold seeds): 2,880 models, with the 720-model snapshot taken at 10 per pair\",\n      \"stop_rule\": \"Timer 36 hours or spend guard: stop before cumulative spend would exceed budget_usd and report the deepest completed level\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"p4_md\",\n      \"what\": \"Refine 20 top cluster representatives with 20 ns explicit-solvent MD and measure interface stability\",\n      \"stop_rule\": \"Timer 8 hours; stop after 20 runs or 6 hours of MD wall time, whichever comes first\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"p5_analysis\",\n      \"what\": \"Bin every pose by capsid symmetry axis and GPI-anchor angle, bootstrap the motif gap at 144, 720 and 2,880 models, write the report\",\n      \"stop_rule\": \"Timer 6 hours; freeze the report at the deepest completed level\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"numbers\": [\n    {\"id\": \"n_capsids\", \"name\": \"capsids in the engineered library\", \"unit\": \"capsids\", \"basis\": \"DESIGN\", \"value\": 12},\n    {\"id\": \"n_receptors\", \"name\": \"BBB receptors in the fixed panel\", \"unit\": \"receptors\", \"basis\": \"DESIGN\", \"value\": 6},\n    {\"id\": \"n_pairs\", \"name\": \"capsid–receptor pairs enumerated\", \"unit\": \"pairs\", \"basis\": \"DERIVED\", \"expr\": \"n_capsids * n_receptors\"},\n    {\"id\": \"n_capsids_ready\", \"name\": \"capsids with usable structures or sequences in p0\", \"unit\": \"capsids\", \"basis\": \"GUESS\", \"value\": 12, \"rests_on\": \"each of the twelve engineered capsids has a published sequence and a parent serotype structure in the AAV capsid catalog\", \"measured_by\": \"p0_inputs\"},\n    {\"id\": \"poses_per_pair_deep\", \"name\": \"pose models per pair at the deep level\", \"unit\": \"pose models\", \"basis\": \"DESIGN\", \"value\": 40},\n    {\"id\": \"n_pose_shallow\", \"name\": \"pose models at the shallow level\", \"unit\": \"pose models\", \"basis\": \"DERIVED\", \"expr\": \"n_pairs * 2\"},\n    {\"id\": \"n_pose_med\", \"name\": \"pose models at the medium level\", \"unit\": \"pose models\", \"basis\": \"DERIVED\", \"expr\": \"n_pairs * 10\"},\n    {\"id\": \"n_pose_deep\", \"name\": \"pose models at the deep level\", \"unit\": \"pose models\", \"basis\": \"DERIVED\", \"expr\": \"n_pairs * poses_per_pair_deep\"},\n    {\"id\": \"af_seeds_deep\", \"name\": \"AlphaFold-Multimer seeds per pair at deep level\", \"unit\": \"seed jobs\", \"basis\": \"DESIGN\", \"value\": 20},\n    {\"id\": \"dock_poses_deep\", \"name\": \"docking poses per pair at deep level\", \"unit\": \"docking poses\", \"basis\": \"DESIGN\", \"value\": 20},\n    {\"id\": \"af_jobs_deep\", \"name\": \"AlphaFold-Multimer jobs at deep level\", \"unit\": \"jobs\", \"basis\": \"DERIVED\", \"expr\": \"n_pairs * af_seeds_deep\"},\n    {\"id\": \"af_job_min\", \"name\": \"wall minutes per AlphaFold-Multimer seed job\", \"unit\": \"minutes\", \"basis\": \"PROXY\", \"value\": 12, \"source_id\": \"s_a100min\", \"quote\": \"Paste a FASTA (monomer or multimer up to 600 aa total) and get pLDDT, PAE, and pTM/ipTM. ~1 to 2 min on A100-40GB.\", \"page_setting\": \"no-MSA single-sequence folding of complexes up to 600 residues on one A100 40GB\", \"differs_in\": [\"ours adds MMseqs2 MSAs, 5 models and up to 20 recycles per job\", \"our complexes are 250 to 400 residues of capsid loop plus receptor ectodomain\"], \"measured_by\": \"p1_pilot\"},\n    {\"id\": \"anchor_job_min\", \"name\": \"wall minutes for the LRP6 anchor job\", \"unit\": \"minutes\", \"basis\": \"GUESS\", \"value\": 30, \"rests_on\": \"the published anchor complex pairs a 1351-residue LRP6 ectodomain with a peptide and is longer than the library jobs scaled from the same runtime proxy\", \"measured_by\": \"p1_pilot\"},\n    {\"id\": \"dock_job_min\", \"name\": \"CPU minutes per global docking job\", \"unit\": \"minutes\", \"basis\": \"GUESS\", \"value\": 30, \"rests_on\": \"global rigid-body search of a 250-residue ectodomain against a VP trimer surface using 16 CPU cores of the instance\", \"measured_by\": \"p1_pilot\"},\n    {\"id\": \"md_ns_per_gpu_day\", \"name\": \"MD throughput for the refinement system\", \"unit\": \"ns per GPU-day\", \"basis\": \"PROXY\", \"value\": 240, \"source_id\": \"s_gmx\", \"quote\": \"A100 | 267.5 | 691.7 | 265.8 | 129.1 | 38.8 | 23.2\", \"page_setting\": \"GROMACS 2024 on one NVIDIA A100, benchmark system 3 (a protein inside a membrane surrounded by explicit water, 80,289 atoms) reaching 265.8 ns/day\", \"differs_in\": [\"our system is about 50,000 atoms of receptor plus capsid loop in water without a membrane\", \"GROMACS version and CPU cores per GPU may differ\"], \"measured_by\": \"p1_pilot\"},\n    {\"id\": \"md_runs\", \"name\": \"MD refinement runs\", \"unit\": \"runs\", \"basis\": \"DESIGN\", \"value\": 20},\n    {\"id\": \"md_ns\", \"name\": \"MD length per refinement run\", \"unit\": \"ns\", \"basis\": \"DESIGN\", \"value\": 20},\n    {\"id\": \"md_atoms\", \"name\": \"atoms per MD refinement system\", \"unit\": \"atoms\", \"basis\": \"DESIGN\", \"value\": 50000},\n    {\"id\": \"storage_gib\", \"name\": \"stored trajectories and models\", \"unit\": \"GiB\", \"basis\": \"DESIGN\", \"value\": 80},\n    {\"id\": \"axis_cutoff_a\", \"name\": \"contact-centroid distance cutoff for the 3-fold class\", \"unit\": \"angstrom\", \"basis\": \"DESIGN\", \"value\": 15},\n    {\"id\": \"gpi_angle_deg\", \"name\": \"max attachment-vector angle for GPI-compatible poses\", \"unit\": \"degrees\", \"basis\": \"DESIGN\", \"value\": 30},\n    {\"id\": \"gap_threshold\", \"name\": \"motif gap rise that counts as compute being the lever\", \"unit\": \"gap\", \"basis\": \"DESIGN\", \"value\": 0.25},\n    {\"id\": \"kappa_min\", \"name\": \"minimum seed-agreement kappa for a resolved pair\", \"unit\": \"kappa\", \"basis\": \"DESIGN\", \"value\": 0.8},\n    {\"id\": \"noise_gap\", \"name\": \"run-to-run noise floor for the motif gap\", \"unit\": \"gap\", \"basis\": \"DESIGN\", \"value\": 0.1},\n    {\"id\": \"anchor_rmsd_a\", \"name\": \"anchor capsid-fragment RMSD tolerance\", \"unit\": \"angstrom\", \"basis\": \"DESIGN\", \"value\": 1.5},\n    {\"id\": \"n_seeds_vote\", \"name\": \"seeds voting per pair in analysis\", \"unit\": \"seeds\", \"basis\": \"DESIGN\", \"value\": 5},\n    {\"id\": \"usd_per_gpu_h_a1008\", \"name\": \"Lambda A100 SXM 40GB price per GPU-hour\", \"unit\": \"usd per GPU-hour\", \"basis\": \"CITED\", \"value\": 1.99, \"source_id\": \"s_lambda\", \"quote\": \"NVIDIA A100 SXM | VRAM/GPU 40 GB | vCPUs 124 | RAM 1800 GiB | STORAGE 5.8 TiB SSD | PRICE/GPU/HR* $1.99\", \"page_setting\": \"Lambda Instances pricing, 8x GPU tab\"},\n    {\"id\": \"instance_h_usd\", \"name\": \"price of one 8x A100 instance-hour\", \"unit\": \"usd per instance-hour\", \"basis\": \"DERIVED\", \"expr\": \"8 * usd_per_gpu_h_a1008\"},\n    {\"id\": \"prior_models_per_peptide\", \"name\": \"AlphaFold models per peptide in the LRP6 study\", \"unit\": \"models\", \"basis\": \"CITED\", \"value\": 5, \"source_id\": \"s_lrp6\", \"quote\": \"Representative AlphaFold models, from 5 structural models each of X1 and CAP-Mac peptides with up to 20 recycles, predict selective interaction with human LRP6 domain E1 (E1 and E2: teal, E3 and E4: yellow, AAV peptides: purple).\", \"page_setting\": \"AlphaFold-Multimer-v3 in ColabFold v2.3.5 for VR-VIII peptides with the LRP6 ectodomain\"},\n    {\"id\": \"prior_peptides\", \"name\": \"capsid peptides modeled in the LRP6 study\", \"unit\": \"peptides\", \"basis\": \"CITED\", \"value\": 2, \"source_id\": \"s_lrp6\", \"quote\": \"The input comprised two sequences: surface-exposed residues in VR-VIII of AAV-X1 (587-AQGNNTRSVAQAQTG-594) or AAV-CAP-Mac (587-AQLNTTKPIAQAQTG-594) and the extracellular domain of human LRP6 (UniProt entry O75581, residues 20-1370).\", \"page_setting\": \"same LRP6 AlphaFold-Multimer study\"},\n    {\"id\": \"prior_models\", \"name\": \"published AlphaFold-Multimer models on this axis\", \"unit\": \"pose models\", \"basis\": \"DERIVED\", \"expr\": \"prior_models_per_peptide * prior_peptides\"}\n  ],\n  \"cost\": {\n    \"rates\": [\n      {\"id\": \"r_a100x8\", \"gpu\": \"NVIDIA A100 SXM\", \"gpu_memory_gb\": 40, \"n_gpus\": 8, \"per_gpu_usd_h\": 1.99},\n      {\"id\": \"r_a100x1\", \"gpu\": \"NVIDIA A100 SXM\", \"gpu_memory_gb\": 40, \"n_gpus\": 1, \"per_gpu_usd_h\": 1.99}\n    ],\n    \"lines\": [\n      {\"id\": \"l_p0_setup\", \"phase\": \"p0_inputs\", \"what\": \"Fetch structures and sequences, write 72 pair FASTAs, run the symmetry-axis precheck\", \"kind\": \"work\", \"rate\": \"r_a100x1\", \"hours\": 2, \"need\": \"1.5\"},\n      {\"id\": \"l_p1_pilot\", \"phase\": \"p1_pilot\", \"what\": \"Anchor reproduction, 6 timed pair jobs, one docking job, 2 ns MD, write pilot/pilot_metrics.txt\", \"kind\": \"work\", \"rate\": \"r_a100x8\", \"hours\": 3, \"need\": \"2.5\"},\n      {\"id\": \"l_p2_shallow\", \"phase\": \"p2_shallow\", \"what\": \"72 pairs at 2 pose models each (144 models) and the first motif gap\", \"kind\": \"work\", \"rate\": \"r_a100x8\", \"hours\": 4, \"need\": \"n_pairs * af_job_min / 60 / 8 + 1\"},\n      {\"id\": \"l_p3_deep\", \"phase\": \"p3_deep\", \"what\": \"Deepen every pair to 40 pose models (2,880 total), with the 720-model snapshot at 10 per pair\", \"kind\": \"work\", \"rate\": \"r_a100x8\", \"hours\": 36, \"need\": \"(af_jobs_deep - n_pairs) * af_job_min / 60 / 8\"},\n      {\"id\": \"l_p4_md\", \"phase\": \"p4_md\", \"what\": \"20 refinements of 20 ns explicit-solvent MD on top cluster representatives\", \"kind\": \"work\", \"rate\": \"r_a100x8\", \"hours\": 8, \"need\": \"md_runs * md_ns / md_ns_per_gpu_day * 24 / 8\"},\n      {\"id\": \"l_p5_analysis\", \"phase\": \"p5_analysis\", \"what\": \"Pose binning by symmetry axis and anchor angle, paired bootstrap of the motif gap, report\", \"kind\": \"work\", \"rate\": \"r_a100x1\", \"hours\": 6, \"need\": \"4\"},\n      {\"id\": \"l_storage\", \"phase\": \"p5_analysis\", \"what\": \"Filesystem storage for trajectories and models for half a month\", \"kind\": \"storage\", \"usd\": \"storage_gib * fs_usd_gib_month * 0.5\"},\n      {\"id\": \"l_contingency\", \"phase\": \"p3_deep\", \"what\": \"Reruns of failed jobs and seed extension on contested pairs\", \"kind\": \"allotment\", \"usd\": 120, \"condition\": \"spent only after the p1_pilot gates pass\"}\n    ],\n    \"scenarios\": [\n      {\"id\": \"scen_slow_jobs\", \"what\": \"Measured jobs run at 25 minutes instead of 12: the p3 gate halves deep seeds to 12 per pair, giving 1,008 deep pose models inside the same 36-hour box\", \"set\": {\"af_job_min\": 25}},\n      {\"id\": \"scen_h100\", \"what\": \"Same work on 8x H100 SXM at $3.99 per GPU-hour: jobs finish about 1.8 times faster, deep line wall-clock near 20 hours, total bill rises to about $1,300\", \"set\": {\"af_job_min\": 7}}\n    ],\n    \"yields\": [\"n_pairs\", \"n_pose_shallow\", \"n_pose_med\", \"n_pose_deep\", \"md_runs\"],\n    \"spend_cap_usd\": 1000,\n    \"total_stated\": 955.84\n  },\n  \"full_scale\": [\n    {\"id\": \"fs_100caps\", \"what\": \"100-capsid library against 6 receptors at 40 pose models each: 24,000 models, 8.3 times the grid here\", \"usd\": \"24000 / 2880 * 573.12\", \"ratio_to\": \"n_pose_deep\"},\n    {\"id\": \"fs_whole_md\", \"what\": \"1 microsecond of all-atom MD for a whole 60-mer capsid with receptor and membrane (about 2.5M atoms, roughly 10 ns/day on one A100)\", \"usd\": \"800 * 15.92\", \"ratio_to\": \"md_ns\"},\n    {\"id\": \"fs_seeds5x\", \"what\": \"200 AlphaFold seeds per pair with Amber relaxation of every pose, five times the deep sampling\", \"usd\": \"5 * 573.12\", \"ratio_to\": \"af_seeds_deep\"}\n  ],\n  \"outside_budget\": [\n    {\"what\": \"Researcher time for construct curation, pipeline setup and analysis\", \"qty\": 40, \"unit\": \"hours\"},\n    {\"what\": \"Public PDB, AlphaFold DB and UniProt downloads and the free MMseqs2 MSA service\", \"qty\": 0, \"unit\": \"usd\"},\n    {\"what\": \"Shared local 4-core machine used only to write this plan; no local compute runs were possible in this session\", \"qty\": 0, \"unit\": \"gpu-hours\"}\n  ],\n  \"restructuring\": {\n    \"sequential_part\": \"None: each capsid–receptor pair is an independent docking and folding job; only short refinements chain within one pair.\",\n    \"method\": \"none\",\n    \"condition\": \"Each AlphaFold or docking job must fit on one A100 40GB and be independent of the others; p1_pilot times 8 parallel jobs against the single-job time to confirm it.\",\n    \"condition_phase\": \"p1_pilot\",\n    \"baseline_sequential\": \"one A100 running all 2,880 models back to back in a single sorted colabfold_batch queue with the JAX compile cache enabled, about 576 GPU-hours or 24 days\",\n    \"baseline_copies\": \"8 independent single-GPU workers on the same 8x A100 instance, the mode the plan actually runs, timed in p1_pilot\"\n  },\n  \"scope_gap\": [\n    \"Endosomal sorting, lysosomal degradation and nuclear import after binding stay untested; computed geometry stands for binding alone.\",\n    \"Whole-capsid motion, receptor glycans and the GPI lipid anchor are approximated rather than simulated.\",\n    \"Twelve capsids and six receptors only; hundreds of published capsids remain unsampled [s_plos].\",\n    \"No new transcytosis assay; correctness rests on published phenotype labels [s_ly6a][s_alpl].\"\n  ],\n  \"novelty\": {\n    \"closest_prior\": \"APPRAISE-AAV ranked capsid peptides against LY6A, LY6C1 and CA4 with AlphaFold-Multimer over ten replicate models per matrix, validating one PHP.eB–LY6A pose [s_appraise].\",\n    \"closest_source_id\": \"s_appraise_rep\",\n    \"prior_max_level\": 10,\n    \"left_open\": \"Whether a shared 3-fold-axis GPI-engagement motif marks transcytosis-competent pairs across a whole capsid panel, or whether deeper pose sampling changes that call [s_appraise].\",\n    \"decides\": \"no\",\n    \"searched\": true\n  },\n  \"limits\": \"Predicted interface geometry only, not transcytosis rates or post-binding fate; weak avidity-dependent contacts may evade prediction [s_appraise]; twelve capsids, six receptors.\",\n  \"test_summary\": \"Run 72 pairs at 144, 720, 2,880 pose models on 8x A100s [s_lambda], anchored on the published PHP.eB–LY6A complex [s_appraise]; compare with the ten-model published baseline and the 144-model shallow arm against phenotype labels [s_alpl].\",\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\"id\": \"s_lrp6\", \"url\": \"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11381518\", \"quote\": \"Representative AlphaFold models, from 5 structural models each of X1 and CAP-Mac peptides with up to 20 recycles, predict selective interaction with human LRP6 domain E1 (E1 and E2: teal, E3 and E4: yellow, AAV peptides: purple).\", \"supports\": \"Prior modeling depth on the pose-model axis: five models per LRP6 peptide complex, two complexes.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"s_lrp6_input\", \"url\": \"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11381518\", \"quote\": \"The input comprised two sequences: surface-exposed residues in VR-VIII of AAV-X1 (587-AQGNNTRSVAQAQTG-594) or AAV-CAP-Mac (587-AQLNTTKPIAQAQTG-594) and the extracellular domain of human LRP6 (UniProt entry O75581, residues 20-1370).\", \"supports\": \"Construct design: capsid VR-VIII peptide against the LRP6 ectodomain; LRP6 E1E2 is the SPR-validated binding fragment.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"s_lrp6_gpu\", \"url\": \"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11381518\", \"quote\": \"We ran the Google Colaboratory notebook using an A100 SXM4 40GB GPU. Five structure models were produced using a protocol with up to 20 recycles, and MSA generated with MMseqs2 (UniRef+Environmental) and templates from PDB70.\", \"supports\": \"Anchor protocol and hardware: one A100 40GB, five models, up to 20 recycles, ColabFold.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"s_cat_vr\", \"url\": \"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12682079\", \"quote\": \"VR-IV, -V, and -VIII interact with each other to form the 3-fold protrusions; and VR-VI and -VII are located at the base of the 3-fold protrusions.\", \"supports\": \"Engineered insertion loops lie on the 3-fold spike, so 3-fold engagement is the motif to test.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"s_cat\", \"url\": \"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12682079\", \"quote\": \"Recombinant Car4 was found to bind to the 3-fold protrusions of AAV9-P31. Due to its size, similar to antibodies bound close to the symmetry axis, a localized cryo-EM reconstruction approach was needed to resolve the complex at 1.8 Å resolution.\", \"supports\": \"Experimental precedent: a GPI-anchored BBB receptor binds the 3-fold protrusions of an engineered AAV capsid.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"s_cat_aavr\", \"url\": \"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12682079\", \"quote\": \"For AAV1, -2, -9, and PHP.eB, the PKD2 domain of AAVR interacted with the capsids in the same binding mode, along the side of the 3-fold protrusions and on top of the 2/5-fold wall\", \"supports\": \"AAVR PKD2 binding mode used for the AAVR construct and pose binning.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"s_cat_count\", \"url\": \"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12682079\", \"quote\": \"To date, 155 AAV capsid structures at a resolution ≤ 4 Å have been determined since 2002\", \"supports\": \"Structures exist to anchor the 12-capsid library.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"s_appraise\", \"url\": \"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10115422\", \"quote\": \"This method uses AlphaFold-Multimer to place surface-exposed peptides spanning mutagenic insertions (AA587 to AA594) from two distinct AAV variants in competition to interact with a potential receptor\", \"supports\": \"Closest prior method: AlphaFold-Multimer peptide–receptor modeling for exactly this receptor question.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"s_appraise_rep\", \"url\": \"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10115422\", \"quote\": \"Matrices ranking AAV peptides by their average competition metric over 10 replicate conditions for LY6A, LY6C1, and mouse CA-IV.\", \"supports\": \"Prior compute level on the pose-model axis: ten replicate models per receptor matrix.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"s_appraise_rmsd\", \"url\": \"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10115422\", \"quote\": \"RMSD (root mean square deviation) between the computational PHP.eB model and a cryo–electron microscopy (cryo-EM)–based model [Protein Data Bank (PDB) ID: 7WQO] is 0.36 Å. RMSD increases in PHP.eB's engineered loop to 1.36 Å.\", \"supports\": \"Anchor value and tolerance: published model sits 0.36 Å from PDB 7WQO, 1.36 Å in the engineered loop.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"s_appraise_contact\", \"url\": \"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10115422\", \"quote\": \"We therefore introduced a point mutation in this groove, LY6A Ala58Arg, without affecting LY6A membrane localization or antibody epitope, and found that it disrupts PHP.eB's enhanced infectivity with the WT receptor (fig. S5B).\", \"supports\": \"Anchor contacts: peptide Pro5'/Phe6' groove and LY6A Ala58 are experimentally validated.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"s_appraise_fail\", \"url\": \"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10115422\", \"quote\": \"AlphaFold-Multimer failed to capture direct contact between fLY6A and PHP.eB capsid in either monomer or trimer configurations.\", \"supports\": \"Limits and expected outcome: whole-capsid contacts evade AlphaFold-Multimer, so integrative placement is required.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"s_appraise_unstable\", \"url\": \"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10115422\", \"quote\": \"Unlike for LY6A and CA-IV, the predicted binding pose for PHP.C2 peptide with LY6C1 was found to vary with the version of AlphaFold-Multimer used, with v1 predictions closely matching mutational data from our cell culture infectivity assay (fig. S6E).\", \"supports\": \"Noise rule and expected outcome: pose predictions for these weak interfaces vary run to run.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"s_appraise_3fold\", \"url\": \"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10115422\", \"quote\": \"To gain a full picture of the AAV-receptor interaction, we next modeled the PHP.eB insertion peptide and LY6A receptor complex within the context of the AAV capsid threefold symmetry spike.\", \"supports\": \"Integrative placement on the 3-fold spike, as this pipeline does.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"s_ly6a\", \"url\": \"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6855452\", \"quote\": \"Interfering with LY6A by CRISPR/Cas9-mediated Ly6a disruption or with blocking antibodies reduced transduction of mouse brain endothelial cells by AAV-PHP.eB, while ectopic expression of Ly6a increased AAV-PHP.eB transduction of HEK293T and CHO cells by 30-fold or more.\", \"supports\": \"Phenotype label: PHP.B/PHP.eB with LY6A is a transcytosis-competent pair.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"s_plos\", \"url\": \"https://journals.plos.org/plosbiology/article?id=10.1371%2Fjournal.pbio.3002112\", \"quote\": \"nearly all published AAV capsids that were selected for their ability to cross the BBB in mice leverage either the LY6A or LY6C1 protein, which are not present in primates\", \"supports\": \"Phenotype labels for LY6A and LY6C1 pairs and the unsampled-capsids scope gap.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"s_alpl\", \"url\": \"https://www.voyagertherapeutics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/POSTER-Voyager_ASGCT_Spring_2024_03_Hoffman_FRIDAY_4-26.pdf\", \"quote\": \"ALPL ectopic expression increased transcytosis of VCAP-102 >100-fold in a transwell model.\", \"supports\": \"Phenotype label: VCAP-102 with ALPL is transcytosis-competent.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"s_alpl_model\", \"url\": \"https://www.voyagertherapeutics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/POSTER-Voyager_ASGCT_Spring_2024_03_Hoffman_FRIDAY_4-26.pdf\", \"quote\": \"In silico modelling predicts the VCAP-102 peptide binds within the catalytic pocket of ALPL, interacting with highly conserved residues.\", \"supports\": \"Published in-silico pose for the VCAP-102–ALPL pair, used as a pose check.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"s_voyager_pr\", \"url\": \"https://ir.voyagertherapeutics.com/news-releases/news-release-details/voyager-therapeutics-presents-data-second-generation-tracertm\", \"quote\": \"To further characterize the mechanism underlying VCAP-102's enhanced brain tropism, Voyager developed a transcytosis model expressing the VCAP-102 receptor in cultured cells and demonstrated that VCAP-102 and second-generation capsids, but not the AAV9 capsid, exhibited efficient transcytosis.\", \"supports\": \"Phenotype labels: VCAP-102 transcytoses while AAV9 does not in the same model.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"s_voyager_gpi\", \"url\": \"https://www.voyagertherapeutics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/BioCentury_Voyagers-journey-to-identify-a-new-shuttle-for-bringing-gene-therapies-into-the-brain.pdf\", \"quote\": \"This really fits with the other receptors that have been identified for novel capsids that have brain tropism,\\\" said Hoffman, as LY6A, LY6C1 and CAIV are all GPI-anchored.\", \"supports\": \"Motif hypothesis: BBB-crossing capsid receptors cluster in the GPI-anchored family.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"s_lambda\", \"url\": \"https://lambda.ai/pricing\", \"quote\": \"NVIDIA A100 SXM | VRAM/GPU 40 GB | vCPUs 124 | RAM 1800 GiB | STORAGE 5.8 TiB SSD | PRICE/GPU/HR* $1.99\", \"supports\": \"Rate: $1.99 per A100 40GB GPU-hour on the 8x instance, and 124 vCPUs for the docking overlay.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"s_gmx\", \"url\": \"https://hpc.fau.de/2024/08/13/gromacs-2024-1-on-brand-new-gpgpus/\", \"quote\": \"A100 | 267.5 | 691.7 | 265.8 | 129.1 | 38.8 | 23.2\", \"supports\": \"MD throughput proxy: 265.8 ns/day on one A100 for an 80,289-atom protein-in-membrane system.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"s_a100min\", \"url\": \"https://tools.ranomics.com/help/tools/colabfold\", \"quote\": \"Paste a FASTA (monomer or multimer up to 600 aa total) and get pLDDT, PAE, and pTM/ipTM. ~1 to 2 min on A100-40GB.\", \"supports\": \"Runtime proxy for one AlphaFold job on an A100 40GB.\"}\n  ],\n  \"files_read\": [\n    \"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11381518\",\n    \"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12682079\",\n    \"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10115422\",\n    \"https://lambda.ai/pricing\",\n    \"https://www.voyagertherapeutics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/POSTER-Voyager_ASGCT_2024_FINAL_Ishan.pdf (fetched; PDF text not extractable in this session, so no claim rests on unverified poster text)\",\n    \"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6855452\",\n    \"https://journals.plos.org/plosbiology/article?id=10.1371%2Fjournal.pbio.3002112\",\n    \"https://www.voyagertherapeutics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/POSTER-Voyager_ASGCT_Spring_2024_03_Hoffman_FRIDAY_4-26.pdf\",\n    \"https://ir.voyagertherapeutics.com/news-releases/news-release-details/voyager-therapeutics-presents-data-second-generation-tracertm\",\n    \"https://www.voyagertherapeutics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/BioCentury_Voyagers-journey-to-identify-a-new-shuttle-for-bringing-gene-therapies-into-the-brain.pdf\",\n    \"https://hpc.fau.de/2024/08/13/gromacs-2024-1-on-brand-new-gpgpus/\",\n    \"https://tools.ranomics.com/help/tools/colabfold\",\n    \"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9184281\",\n    \"producer.md (written this session)\",\n    \"pilot/run_pilot.py (written this session; executed later by phase p1_pilot on the Lambda instance)\"\n  ]\n}\n","filePath":"/home/hal/dev/interp/metis/experiments/blind-01/20261021-0116-loop/out/r0/card/work/seed-1/seed/idea/55c57ced/producer.md"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/home/hal/dev/interp/metis/experiments/blind-01/20261021-0116-loop/out/r0/card/work/seed-1/seed/idea/55c57ced/producer.md","exists":true,"truncated":false},"title":"experiments/blind-01/20261021-0116-loop/out/r0/card/work/seed-1/seed/idea/55c57ced/producer.md","time":{"start":1792549084138,"end":1792549084178}},"id":"prt_15c3e3afa001ckeahcjg2dm9wX","sessionID":"ses_ea3e01b08ffe25JrGjIjfiH29d","messageID":"msg_15c3b6f74001mW1jY55fjO6g7B"}}
