{"type":"text","timestamp":1792549297809,"sessionID":"ses_ea3e01b08ffe25JrGjIjfiH29d","part":{"id":"prt_15c41d412001HlBIKmbpR0zCbI","messageID":"msg_15c41af75001WJKwjQ5ZqMun5W","sessionID":"ses_ea3e01b08ffe25JrGjIjfiH29d","type":"text","text":"{\"option_title\":\"Exhaustive capsid–receptor complex enumeration (docking and AlphaFold-Multimer)\",\"question\":\"Does exhaustive modeling of AAV capsid–receptor complexes reveal a shared interface motif, like 3-fold-axis GPI-receptor engagement, that marks which capsids transcytose the BBB?\",\"hypothesis\":\"Transcytosis-competent capsids engage GPI-anchored BBB receptors at the capsid 3-fold spike with a shared anchor geometry, unlike non-cognate pairs [s_appraise].\",\"compute_axis\":{\"quantity\":\"capsid–receptor pose models computed per panel sweep (rigid-docking poses plus AlphaFold-Multimer seed models)\",\"unit\":\"pose models\",\"levels\":[144,720,2880]},\"held_fixed\":[\"the 12-capsid library (AAV9, AAV2, PHP.B, PHP.eB, PHP.eC, 9P31, 9P36, VCAP-102, AAV9-X1.1, CAP-Mac, CAP-B22, AAV-BI30)\",\"the 6-receptor panel (LY6A, LY6C1, ALPL, LRP6 E1E2, CA4, AAVR PKD2)\",\"constructs: capsid VR-IV plus VR-VIII loops against receptor ectodomains\",\"ColabFold v2.3.5 AlphaFold-Multimer-v3 settings: 5 models, up to 20 recycles, MMseqs2 MSAs [s_lrp6_gpu]\",\"docking search space: VP trimer with the insertion loop as anchor\",\"motif definition: contact centroid within 15 Å of the 3-fold axis, GPI anchor vector within 30° of the membrane normal\",\"published phenotype labels used for scoring\",\"8x NVIDIA A100 SXM 40GB instances at $1.99 per GPU-hour [s_lambda]\"],\"predictions\":{\"if_lever\":\"At 2,880 models the competent-minus-retained GPI-engagement gap reaches 0.50 or more, while at 144 models it stays below 0.25.\",\"if_not\":\"The gap stays within 0.15 of its 144-model value at every depth; added poses change nothing because insert location already fixes the 3-fold site [s_cat].\",\"decision_rule\":\"Paired comparison of the motif gap at 2,880 versus 144 models on the same 72 pairs: call if_lever if the gap rises by at least 0.25 with disjoint bootstrap 95% intervals; call if_not if it moves less than 0.15 and per-pair seed agreement kappa is at least 0.8; otherwise unsure.\",\"noise_rule\":\"Five AlphaFold seeds per pair vote on motif class, pairs with kappa below 0.8 are unresolved; paired bootstrap over 72 pairs gives intervals; a fresh-seed medium rerun must reproduce the gap within 0.10.\",\"expected\":\"if_not\",\"expected_why\":\"Capsid insertions already sit on the 3-fold spike [s_cat] and AlphaFold-Multimer poses for these weak interfaces vary by run and version [s_appraise_unstable], so extra poses add noise rather than a converged signature.\"},\"compute_tested\":\"yes\",\"compute_tested_why\":\"Each pose model is an independent docking or AlphaFold-Multimer job with its own seed, so the model count of 144, 720 or 2,880 is exactly what extra parallel GPUs buy.\",\"scored_against\":\"Published capsid–receptor phenotype labels: PHP.B/PHP.eB–LY6A and VCAP-102–ALPL transcytosis versus AAV9 and AAV2 retention [s_ly6a][s_alpl][s_voyager_pr], plus the published PHP.eB–LY6A binding pose and contacts [s_appraise_rmsd].\",\"arms\":[{\"id\":\"arm_shallow\",\"what\":\"72 pairs at 2 pose models each (1 docking pose plus 1 AlphaFold seed): 144 models; first motif gap\"},{\"id\":\"arm_medium\",\"what\":\"Same 72 pairs at 10 pose models each: 720 models; the intermediate snapshot\"},{\"id\":\"arm_deep\",\"what\":\"Same 72 pairs at 40 pose models each (20 docking poses plus 20 AlphaFold seeds): 2,880 models\"},{\"id\":\"arm_md\",\"what\":\"20 explicit-solvent MD refinements of 20 ns on top cluster representatives\"},{\"id\":\"arm_anchor\",\"what\":\"Reproduction of the published PHP.eB peptide–LY6A complex and the LRP6–X1 peptide complex before library spend\"},{\"id\":\"arm_controls\",\"what\":\"Negative control: a non-receptor protein run against 12 capsids at shallow depth to measure the hallucination rate\"}],\"baseline\":{\"what\":\"Published depth for this computation: ten AlphaFold-Multimer models per receptor competition matrix [s_appraise_rep] and two LRP6 peptide complexes with five models each [s_lrp6]; the minimal arm here is one pose model per pair.\",\"value\":10,\"source_id\":\"s_appraise_rep\"},\"anchor\":{\"what\":\"Rebuild the published PHP.eB peptide–LY6A complex and require its validated contacts and capsid fit before any library spend [s_appraise].\",\"published_value\":0.36,\"tolerance\":\"capsid-fragment RMSD to PDB 7WQO at most 1.5 Å (published engineered-loop RMSD is 1.36 Å) and at least 2 of the 3 named contacts (peptide Pro5', Phe6', LY6A Ala58) within 5 Å\",\"source_id\":\"s_appraise_rmsd\",\"independent_code\":\"the RosettaRemodel integrative pipeline of Shay et al. 2023 [s_appraise_3fold], run apart from our ColabFold-plus-docking pipeline\"},\"checks\":[\"Anchor first: PHP.eB–LY6A rerun must reproduce Pro5'/Phe6' and LY6A Ala58 contacts within 5 Å and capsid RMSD to 7WQO within 1.5 Å before any library spend [s_appraise_rmsd].\",\"Positive controls: cognate pairs PHP.eB–LY6A, 9P31–CA4, VCAP-102–ALPL and AAV9-X1.1–LRP6 must rank in the top quartile of interface confidence [s_ly6a][s_cat][s_alpl][s_lrp6].\",\"Negative control: a non-receptor protein against 12 capsids at shallow depth must not yield stable 3-fold motif calls above 20 percent.\",\"AAV9 and AAV2 must show no stable LY6A pose; AAV9 is a published non-binder [s_appraise].\",\"Seed stability: motif class unchanged across at least 4 of 5 seeds (kappa at least 0.8); unstable pairs marked unresolved rather than forced.\",\"MD stability: refined pose interface backbone RMSD below 3 Å over 20 ns.\",\"Noise floor: a fresh-seed medium rerun reproduces the motif gap within 0.10.\",\"GPI geometry: receptor C-terminal attachment vector within 30° of the membrane normal in every pose counted as GPI-engaging.\"],\"phases\":[{\"id\":\"p0_inputs\",\"what\":\"Fetch 12 capsid and 6 receptor constructs, build the 72 pair FASTAs, run the symmetry-axis precheck that each engineered insertion lies on the 3-fold spike [s_cat_vr]\",\"gate\":{\"on\":\"n_capsids_ready\",\"op\":\">=\",\"value\":9,\"else\":\"shrink the library to ready capsids, re-derive the pair grid and re-price before any GPU spend\"}},{\"id\":\"p1_pilot\",\"what\":\"On one 8x A100 instance: reproduce the PHP.eB–LY6A anchor, time 6 representative pair jobs, one docking job and 2 ns MD, write pilot/pilot_metrics.txt with pilot/run_pilot.py\",\"stop_rule\":\"Timer 3 hours; no library spend until the anchor contacts reproduce\",\"gate\":{\"on\":\"af_job_min\",\"op\":\"<=\",\"value\":20,\"else\":\"halve af_seeds_deep to 12 per pair and re-price; stop entirely if jobs exceed 30 min\"}},{\"id\":\"p2_shallow\",\"what\":\"Compute 2 pose models for every pair (1 docking pose plus 1 AlphaFold seed): 144 models, and the first motif gap\",\"stop_rule\":\"Timer 4 hours; deliver the 144-model snapshot even if some pairs have fewer poses (mark them unresolved)\"},{\"id\":\"p3_deep\",\"what\":\"Deepen each pair to 40 pose models (20 docking poses plus 20 AlphaFold seeds): 2,880 models, with the 720-model snapshot taken at 10 per pair\",\"stop_rule\":\"Timer 36 hours or spend guard: stop before cumulative spend would exceed budget_usd and report the deepest completed level\"},{\"id\":\"p4_md\",\"what\":\"Refine 20 top cluster representatives with 20 ns explicit-solvent MD and measure interface stability\",\"stop_rule\":\"Timer 8 hours; stop after 20 runs or 6 hours of MD wall time, whichever comes first\"},{\"id\":\"p5_analysis\",\"what\":\"Bin every pose by capsid symmetry axis and GPI-anchor angle, bootstrap the motif gap at 144, 720 and 2,880 models, write the report\",\"stop_rule\":\"Timer 6 hours; freeze the report at the deepest completed level\"}],\"numbers\":[{\"id\":\"n_capsids\",\"name\":\"capsids in the engineered library\",\"unit\":\"capsids\",\"basis\":\"DESIGN\",\"value\":12},{\"id\":\"n_receptors\",\"name\":\"BBB receptors in the fixed panel\",\"unit\":\"receptors\",\"basis\":\"DESIGN\",\"value\":6},{\"id\":\"n_pairs\",\"name\":\"capsid–receptor pairs enumerated\",\"unit\":\"pairs\",\"basis\":\"DERIVED\",\"expr\":\"n_capsids * n_receptors\"},{\"id\":\"n_capsids_ready\",\"name\":\"capsids with usable structures or sequences in p0\",\"unit\":\"capsids\",\"basis\":\"GUESS\",\"value\":12,\"rests_on\":\"each of the twelve engineered capsids has a published sequence and a parent serotype structure in the AAV capsid catalog\",\"measured_by\":\"p0_inputs\"},{\"id\":\"poses_per_pair_deep\",\"name\":\"pose models per pair at the deep level\",\"unit\":\"pose models\",\"basis\":\"DESIGN\",\"value\":40},{\"id\":\"n_pose_shallow\",\"name\":\"pose models at the shallow level\",\"unit\":\"pose models\",\"basis\":\"DERIVED\",\"expr\":\"n_pairs * 2\"},{\"id\":\"n_pose_med\",\"name\":\"pose models at the medium level\",\"unit\":\"pose models\",\"basis\":\"DERIVED\",\"expr\":\"n_pairs * 10\"},{\"id\":\"n_pose_deep\",\"name\":\"pose models at the deep level\",\"unit\":\"pose models\",\"basis\":\"DERIVED\",\"expr\":\"n_pairs * poses_per_pair_deep\"},{\"id\":\"af_seeds_deep\",\"name\":\"AlphaFold-Multimer seeds per pair at deep level\",\"unit\":\"seed jobs\",\"basis\":\"DESIGN\",\"value\":20},{\"id\":\"dock_poses_deep\",\"name\":\"docking poses per pair at deep level\",\"unit\":\"docking poses\",\"basis\":\"DESIGN\",\"value\":20},{\"id\":\"af_jobs_deep\",\"name\":\"AlphaFold-Multimer jobs at deep level\",\"unit\":\"jobs\",\"basis\":\"DERIVED\",\"expr\":\"n_pairs * af_seeds_deep\"},{\"id\":\"af_job_min\",\"name\":\"wall minutes per AlphaFold-Multimer seed job\",\"unit\":\"minutes\",\"basis\":\"PROXY\",\"value\":12,\"source_id\":\"s_a100min\",\"quote\":\"Paste a FASTA (monomer or multimer up to 600 aa total) and get pLDDT, PAE, and pTM/ipTM. ~1 to 2 min on A100-40GB.\",\"page_setting\":\"no-MSA single-sequence folding of complexes up to 600 residues on one A100 40GB\",\"differs_in\":[\"ours adds MMseqs2 MSAs, 5 models and up to 20 recycles per job\",\"our complexes are 250 to 400 residues of capsid loop plus receptor ectodomain\"],\"measured_by\":\"p1_pilot\"},{\"id\":\"anchor_job_min\",\"name\":\"wall minutes for the LRP6 anchor job\",\"unit\":\"minutes\",\"basis\":\"GUESS\",\"value\":30,\"rests_on\":\"the published anchor complex pairs a 1351-residue LRP6 ectodomain with a peptide and is longer than the library jobs scaled from the same runtime proxy\",\"measured_by\":\"p1_pilot\"},{\"id\":\"dock_job_min\",\"name\":\"CPU minutes per global docking job\",\"unit\":\"minutes\",\"basis\":\"GUESS\",\"value\":30,\"rests_on\":\"global rigid-body search of a 250-residue ectodomain against a VP trimer surface using 16 CPU cores of the instance\",\"measured_by\":\"p1_pilot\"},{\"id\":\"md_ns_per_gpu_day\",\"name\":\"MD throughput for the refinement system\",\"unit\":\"ns per GPU-day\",\"basis\":\"PROXY\",\"value\":240,\"source_id\":\"s_gmx\",\"quote\":\"A100 | 267.5 | 691.7 | 265.8 | 129.1 | 38.8 | 23.2\",\"page_setting\":\"GROMACS 2024 on one NVIDIA A100, benchmark system 3 (a protein inside a membrane surrounded by explicit water, 80,289 atoms) reaching 265.8 ns/day\",\"differs_in\":[\"our system is about 50,000 atoms of receptor plus capsid loop in water without a membrane\",\"GROMACS version and CPU cores per GPU may differ\"],\"measured_by\":\"p1_pilot\"},{\"id\":\"md_runs\",\"name\":\"MD refinement runs\",\"unit\":\"runs\",\"basis\":\"DESIGN\",\"value\":20},{\"id\":\"md_ns\",\"name\":\"MD length per refinement run\",\"unit\":\"ns\",\"basis\":\"DESIGN\",\"value\":20},{\"id\":\"md_atoms\",\"name\":\"atoms per MD refinement system\",\"unit\":\"atoms\",\"basis\":\"DESIGN\",\"value\":50000},{\"id\":\"storage_gib\",\"name\":\"stored trajectories and models\",\"unit\":\"GiB\",\"basis\":\"DESIGN\",\"value\":80},{\"id\":\"axis_cutoff_a\",\"name\":\"contact-centroid distance cutoff for the 3-fold class\",\"unit\":\"angstrom\",\"basis\":\"DESIGN\",\"value\":15},{\"id\":\"gpi_angle_deg\",\"name\":\"max attachment-vector angle for GPI-compatible poses\",\"unit\":\"degrees\",\"basis\":\"DESIGN\",\"value\":30},{\"id\":\"gap_threshold\",\"name\":\"motif gap rise that counts as compute being the lever\",\"unit\":\"gap\",\"basis\":\"DESIGN\",\"value\":0.25},{\"id\":\"kappa_min\",\"name\":\"minimum seed-agreement kappa for a resolved pair\",\"unit\":\"kappa\",\"basis\":\"DESIGN\",\"value\":0.8},{\"id\":\"noise_gap\",\"name\":\"run-to-run noise floor for the motif gap\",\"unit\":\"gap\",\"basis\":\"DESIGN\",\"value\":0.1},{\"id\":\"anchor_rmsd_a\",\"name\":\"anchor capsid-fragment RMSD tolerance\",\"unit\":\"angstrom\",\"basis\":\"DESIGN\",\"value\":1.5},{\"id\":\"n_seeds_vote\",\"name\":\"seeds voting per pair in analysis\",\"unit\":\"seeds\",\"basis\":\"DESIGN\",\"value\":5},{\"id\":\"usd_per_gpu_h_a1008\",\"name\":\"Lambda A100 SXM 40GB price per GPU-hour\",\"unit\":\"usd per GPU-hour\",\"basis\":\"CITED\",\"value\":1.99,\"source_id\":\"s_lambda\",\"quote\":\"NVIDIA A100 SXM | VRAM/GPU 40 GB | vCPUs 124 | RAM 1800 GiB | STORAGE 5.8 TiB SSD | PRICE/GPU/HR* $1.99\",\"page_setting\":\"Lambda Instances pricing, 8x GPU tab\"},{\"id\":\"instance_h_usd\",\"name\":\"price of one 8x A100 instance-hour\",\"unit\":\"usd per instance-hour\",\"basis\":\"DERIVED\",\"expr\":\"8 * usd_per_gpu_h_a1008\"},{\"id\":\"prior_models_per_peptide\",\"name\":\"AlphaFold models per peptide in the LRP6 study\",\"unit\":\"models\",\"basis\":\"CITED\",\"value\":5,\"source_id\":\"s_lrp6\",\"quote\":\"Representative AlphaFold models, from 5 structural models each of X1 and CAP-Mac peptides with up to 20 recycles, predict selective interaction with human LRP6 domain E1 (E1 and E2: teal, E3 and E4: yellow, AAV peptides: purple).\",\"page_setting\":\"AlphaFold-Multimer-v3 in ColabFold v2.3.5 for VR-VIII peptides with the LRP6 ectodomain\"},{\"id\":\"prior_peptides\",\"name\":\"capsid peptides modeled in the LRP6 study\",\"unit\":\"peptides\",\"basis\":\"CITED\",\"value\":2,\"source_id\":\"s_lrp6\",\"quote\":\"The input comprised two sequences: surface-exposed residues in VR-VIII of AAV-X1 (587-AQGNNTRSVAQAQTG-594) or AAV-CAP-Mac (587-AQLNTTKPIAQAQTG-594) and the extracellular domain of human LRP6 (UniProt entry O75581, residues 20-1370).\",\"page_setting\":\"same LRP6 AlphaFold-Multimer study\"},{\"id\":\"prior_models\",\"name\":\"published AlphaFold-Multimer models on this axis\",\"unit\":\"pose models\",\"basis\":\"DERIVED\",\"expr\":\"prior_models_per_peptide * prior_peptides\"}],\"cost\":{\"rates\":[{\"id\":\"r_a100x8\",\"gpu\":\"NVIDIA A100 SXM\",\"gpu_memory_gb\":40,\"n_gpus\":8,\"per_gpu_usd_h\":1.99},{\"id\":\"r_a100x1\",\"gpu\":\"NVIDIA A100 SXM\",\"gpu_memory_gb\":40,\"n_gpus\":1,\"per_gpu_usd_h\":1.99}],\"lines\":[{\"id\":\"l_p0_setup\",\"phase\":\"p0_inputs\",\"what\":\"Fetch structures and sequences, write 72 pair FASTAs, run the symmetry-axis precheck\",\"kind\":\"work\",\"rate\":\"r_a100x1\",\"hours\":2,\"need\":\"1.5\"},{\"id\":\"l_p1_pilot\",\"phase\":\"p1_pilot\",\"what\":\"Anchor reproduction, 6 timed pair jobs, one docking job, 2 ns MD, write pilot/pilot_metrics.txt\",\"kind\":\"work\",\"rate\":\"r_a100x8\",\"hours\":3,\"need\":\"2.5\"},{\"id\":\"l_p2_shallow\",\"phase\":\"p2_shallow\",\"what\":\"72 pairs at 2 pose models each (144 models) and the first motif gap\",\"kind\":\"work\",\"rate\":\"r_a100x8\",\"hours\":4,\"need\":\"n_pairs * af_job_min / 60 / 8 + 1\"},{\"id\":\"l_p3_deep\",\"phase\":\"p3_deep\",\"what\":\"Deepen every pair to 40 pose models (2,880 total), with the 720-model snapshot at 10 per pair\",\"kind\":\"work\",\"rate\":\"r_a100x8\",\"hours\":36,\"need\":\"(af_jobs_deep - n_pairs) * af_job_min / 60 / 8\"},{\"id\":\"l_p4_md\",\"phase\":\"p4_md\",\"what\":\"20 refinements of 20 ns explicit-solvent MD on top cluster representatives\",\"kind\":\"work\",\"rate\":\"r_a100x8\",\"hours\":8,\"need\":\"md_runs * md_ns / md_ns_per_gpu_day * 24 / 8\"},{\"id\":\"l_p5_analysis\",\"phase\":\"p5_analysis\",\"what\":\"Pose binning by symmetry axis and anchor angle, paired bootstrap of the motif gap, report\",\"kind\":\"work\",\"rate\":\"r_a100x1\",\"hours\":6,\"need\":\"4\"},{\"id\":\"l_storage\",\"phase\":\"p5_analysis\",\"what\":\"Filesystem storage for trajectories and models for half a month\",\"kind\":\"storage\",\"usd\":\"storage_gib * fs_usd_gib_month * 0.5\"},{\"id\":\"l_contingency\",\"phase\":\"p3_deep\",\"what\":\"Reruns of failed jobs and seed extension on contested pairs\",\"kind\":\"allotment\",\"usd\":120,\"condition\":\"spent only after the p1_pilot gates pass\"}],\"scenarios\":[{\"id\":\"scen_slow_jobs\",\"what\":\"Measured jobs run at 25 minutes instead of 12: the p3 gate halves deep seeds to 12 per pair, giving 1,008 deep pose models inside the same 36-hour box\",\"set\":{\"af_job_min\":25}},{\"id\":\"scen_h100\",\"what\":\"Same work on 8x H100 SXM at $3.99 per GPU-hour: jobs finish about 1.8 times faster, deep line wall-clock near 20 hours, total bill rises to about $1,300\",\"set\":{\"af_job_min\":7}}],\"yields\":[\"n_pairs\",\"n_pose_shallow\",\"n_pose_med\",\"n_pose_deep\",\"md_runs\"],\"spend_cap_usd\":1000,\"total_stated\":955.84},\"full_scale\":[{\"id\":\"fs_100caps\",\"what\":\"100-capsid library against 6 receptors at 40 pose models each: 24,000 models, 8.3 times the grid here\",\"usd\":\"24000 / 2880 * 573.12\",\"ratio_to\":\"n_pose_deep\"},{\"id\":\"fs_whole_md\",\"what\":\"1 microsecond of all-atom MD for a whole 60-mer capsid with receptor and membrane (about 2.5M atoms, roughly 10 ns/day on one A100)\",\"usd\":\"800 * 15.92\",\"ratio_to\":\"md_ns\"},{\"id\":\"fs_seeds5x\",\"what\":\"200 AlphaFold seeds per pair with Amber relaxation of every pose, five times the deep sampling\",\"usd\":\"5 * 573.12\",\"ratio_to\":\"af_seeds_deep\"}],\"outside_budget\":[{\"what\":\"Researcher time for construct curation, pipeline setup and analysis\",\"qty\":40,\"unit\":\"hours\"},{\"what\":\"Public PDB, AlphaFold DB and UniProt downloads and the free MMseqs2 MSA service\",\"qty\":0,\"unit\":\"usd\"},{\"what\":\"Shared local 4-core machine used only to write this plan; no local compute runs were possible in this session\",\"qty\":0,\"unit\":\"gpu-hours\"}],\"restructuring\":{\"sequential_part\":\"None: each capsid–receptor pair is an independent docking and folding job; only short refinements chain within one pair.\",\"method\":\"none\",\"condition\":\"Each AlphaFold or docking job must fit on one A100 40GB and be independent of the others; p1_pilot times 8 parallel jobs against the single-job time to confirm it.\",\"condition_phase\":\"p1_pilot\",\"baseline_sequential\":\"one A100 running all 2,880 models back to back in a single sorted colabfold_batch queue with the JAX compile cache enabled, about 576 GPU-hours or 24 days\",\"baseline_copies\":\"8 independent single-GPU workers on the same 8x A100 instance, the mode the plan actually runs, timed in p1_pilot\"},\"scope_gap\":[\"Endosomal sorting, lysosomal degradation and nuclear import after binding stay untested; computed geometry stands for binding alone.\",\"Whole-capsid motion, receptor glycans and the GPI lipid anchor are approximated rather than simulated.\",\"Twelve capsids and six receptors only; hundreds of published capsids remain unsampled [s_plos].\",\"No new transcytosis assay; correctness rests on published phenotype labels [s_ly6a][s_alpl].\"],\"novelty\":{\"closest_prior\":\"APPRAISE-AAV ranked capsid peptides against LY6A, LY6C1 and CA4 with AlphaFold-Multimer over ten replicate models per matrix, validating one PHP.eB–LY6A pose [s_appraise].\",\"closest_source_id\":\"s_appraise_rep\",\"prior_max_level\":10,\"left_open\":\"Whether a shared 3-fold-axis GPI-engagement motif marks transcytosis-competent pairs across a whole capsid panel, or whether deeper pose sampling changes that call [s_appraise].\",\"decides\":\"no\",\"searched\":true},\"limits\":\"Predicted interface geometry only, not transcytosis rates or post-binding fate; weak avidity-dependent contacts may evade prediction [s_appraise]; twelve capsids, six receptors.\",\"test_summary\":\"Run 72 pairs at 144, 720, 2,880 pose models on 8x A100s [s_lambda], anchored on the published PHP.eB–LY6A complex [s_appraise]; compare with the ten-model published baseline and the 144-model shallow arm against phenotype labels [s_alpl].\",\"sources\":[{\"id\":\"s_lrp6\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11381518\",\"quote\":\"Representative AlphaFold models, from 5 structural models each of X1 and CAP-Mac peptides with up to 20 recycles, predict selective interaction with human LRP6 domain E1 (E1 and E2: teal, E3 and E4: yellow, AAV peptides: purple).\",\"supports\":\"Prior modeling depth on the pose-model axis: five models per LRP6 peptide complex, two complexes.\"},{\"id\":\"s_lrp6_input\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11381518\",\"quote\":\"The input comprised two sequences: surface-exposed residues in VR-VIII of AAV-X1 (587-AQGNNTRSVAQAQTG-594) or AAV-CAP-Mac (587-AQLNTTKPIAQAQTG-594) and the extracellular domain of human LRP6 (UniProt entry O75581, residues 20-1370).\",\"supports\":\"Construct design: capsid VR-VIII peptide against the LRP6 ectodomain; LRP6 E1E2 is the SPR-validated binding fragment.\"},{\"id\":\"s_lrp6_gpu\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11381518\",\"quote\":\"We ran the Google Colaboratory notebook using an A100 SXM4 40GB GPU. Five structure models were produced using a protocol with up to 20 recycles, and MSA generated with MMseqs2 (UniRef+Environmental) and templates from PDB70.\",\"supports\":\"Anchor protocol and hardware: one A100 40GB, five models, up to 20 recycles, ColabFold.\"},{\"id\":\"s_cat_vr\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12682079\",\"quote\":\"VR-IV, -V, and -VIII interact with each other to form the 3-fold protrusions; and VR-VI and -VII are located at the base of the 3-fold protrusions.\",\"supports\":\"Engineered insertion loops lie on the 3-fold spike, so 3-fold engagement is the motif to test.\"},{\"id\":\"s_cat\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12682079\",\"quote\":\"Recombinant Car4 was found to bind to the 3-fold protrusions of AAV9-P31. Due to its size, similar to antibodies bound close to the symmetry axis, a localized cryo-EM reconstruction approach was needed to resolve the complex at 1.8 Å resolution.\",\"supports\":\"Experimental precedent: a GPI-anchored BBB receptor binds the 3-fold protrusions of an engineered AAV capsid.\"},{\"id\":\"s_cat_aavr\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12682079\",\"quote\":\"For AAV1, -2, -9, and PHP.eB, the PKD2 domain of AAVR interacted with the capsids in the same binding mode, along the side of the 3-fold protrusions and on top of the 2/5-fold wall\",\"supports\":\"AAVR PKD2 binding mode used for the AAVR construct and pose binning.\"},{\"id\":\"s_cat_count\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12682079\",\"quote\":\"To date, 155 AAV capsid structures at a resolution ≤ 4 Å have been determined since 2002\",\"supports\":\"Structures exist to anchor the 12-capsid library.\"},{\"id\":\"s_appraise\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10115422\",\"quote\":\"This method uses AlphaFold-Multimer to place surface-exposed peptides spanning mutagenic insertions (AA587 to AA594) from two distinct AAV variants in competition to interact with a potential receptor\",\"supports\":\"Closest prior method: AlphaFold-Multimer peptide–receptor modeling for exactly this receptor question.\"},{\"id\":\"s_appraise_rep\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10115422\",\"quote\":\"Matrices ranking AAV peptides by their average competition metric over 10 replicate conditions for LY6A, LY6C1, and mouse CA-IV.\",\"supports\":\"Prior compute level on the pose-model axis: ten replicate models per receptor matrix.\"},{\"id\":\"s_appraise_rmsd\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10115422\",\"quote\":\"RMSD (root mean square deviation) between the computational PHP.eB model and a cryo–electron microscopy (cryo-EM)–based model [Protein Data Bank (PDB) ID: 7WQO] is 0.36 Å. RMSD increases in PHP.eB's engineered loop to 1.36 Å.\",\"supports\":\"Anchor value and tolerance: published model sits 0.36 Å from PDB 7WQO, 1.36 Å in the engineered loop.\"},{\"id\":\"s_appraise_contact\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10115422\",\"quote\":\"We therefore introduced a point mutation in this groove, LY6A Ala58Arg, without affecting LY6A membrane localization or antibody epitope, and found that it disrupts PHP.eB's enhanced infectivity with the WT receptor (fig. S5B).\",\"supports\":\"Anchor contacts: peptide Pro5'/Phe6' groove and LY6A Ala58 are experimentally validated.\"},{\"id\":\"s_appraise_fail\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10115422\",\"quote\":\"AlphaFold-Multimer failed to capture direct contact between fLY6A and PHP.eB capsid in either monomer or trimer configurations.\",\"supports\":\"Limits and expected outcome: whole-capsid contacts evade AlphaFold-Multimer, so integrative placement is required.\"},{\"id\":\"s_appraise_unstable\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10115422\",\"quote\":\"Unlike for LY6A and CA-IV, the predicted binding pose for PHP.C2 peptide with LY6C1 was found to vary with the version of AlphaFold-Multimer used, with v1 predictions closely matching mutational data from our cell culture infectivity assay (fig. S6E).\",\"supports\":\"Noise rule and expected outcome: pose predictions for these weak interfaces vary run to run.\"},{\"id\":\"s_appraise_3fold\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10115422\",\"quote\":\"To gain a full picture of the AAV-receptor interaction, we next modeled the PHP.eB insertion peptide and LY6A receptor complex within the context of the AAV capsid threefold symmetry spike.\",\"supports\":\"Integrative placement on the 3-fold spike, as this pipeline does.\"},{\"id\":\"s_ly6a\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6855452\",\"quote\":\"Interfering with LY6A by CRISPR/Cas9-mediated Ly6a disruption or with blocking antibodies reduced transduction of mouse brain endothelial cells by AAV-PHP.eB, while ectopic expression of Ly6a increased AAV-PHP.eB transduction of HEK293T and CHO cells by 30-fold or more.\",\"supports\":\"Phenotype label: PHP.B/PHP.eB with LY6A is a transcytosis-competent pair.\"},{\"id\":\"s_plos\",\"url\":\"https://journals.plos.org/plosbiology/article?id=10.1371%2Fjournal.pbio.3002112\",\"quote\":\"nearly all published AAV capsids that were selected for their ability to cross the BBB in mice leverage either the LY6A or LY6C1 protein, which are not present in primates\",\"supports\":\"Phenotype labels for LY6A and LY6C1 pairs and the unsampled-capsids scope gap.\"},{\"id\":\"s_alpl\",\"url\":\"https://www.voyagertherapeutics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/POSTER-Voyager_ASGCT_Spring_2024_03_Hoffman_FRIDAY_4-26.pdf\",\"quote\":\"ALPL ectopic expression increased transcytosis of VCAP-102 >100-fold in a transwell model.\",\"supports\":\"Phenotype label: VCAP-102 with ALPL is transcytosis-competent.\"},{\"id\":\"s_alpl_model\",\"url\":\"https://www.voyagertherapeutics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/POSTER-Voyager_ASGCT_Spring_2024_03_Hoffman_FRIDAY_4-26.pdf\",\"quote\":\"In silico modelling predicts the VCAP-102 peptide binds within the catalytic pocket of ALPL, interacting with highly conserved residues.\",\"supports\":\"Published in-silico pose for the VCAP-102–ALPL pair, used as a pose check.\"},{\"id\":\"s_voyager_pr\",\"url\":\"https://ir.voyagertherapeutics.com/news-releases/news-release-details/voyager-therapeutics-presents-data-second-generation-tracertm\",\"quote\":\"To further characterize the mechanism underlying VCAP-102's enhanced brain tropism, Voyager developed a transcytosis model expressing the VCAP-102 receptor in cultured cells and demonstrated that VCAP-102 and second-generation capsids, but not the AAV9 capsid, exhibited efficient transcytosis.\",\"supports\":\"Phenotype labels: VCAP-102 transcytoses while AAV9 does not in the same model.\"},{\"id\":\"s_voyager_gpi\",\"url\":\"https://www.voyagertherapeutics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/BioCentury_Voyagers-journey-to-identify-a-new-shuttle-for-bringing-gene-therapies-into-the-brain.pdf\",\"quote\":\"This really fits with the other receptors that have been identified for novel capsids that have brain tropism,\\\" said Hoffman, as LY6A, LY6C1 and CAIV are all GPI-anchored.\",\"supports\":\"Motif hypothesis: BBB-crossing capsid receptors cluster in the GPI-anchored family.\"},{\"id\":\"s_lambda\",\"url\":\"https://lambda.ai/pricing\",\"quote\":\"NVIDIA A100 SXM | VRAM/GPU 40 GB | vCPUs 124 | RAM 1800 GiB | STORAGE 5.8 TiB SSD | PRICE/GPU/HR* $1.99\",\"supports\":\"Rate: $1.99 per A100 40GB GPU-hour on the 8x instance, and 124 vCPUs for the docking overlay.\"},{\"id\":\"s_gmx\",\"url\":\"https://hpc.fau.de/2024/08/13/gromacs-2024-1-on-brand-new-gpgpus/\",\"quote\":\"A100 | 267.5 | 691.7 | 265.8 | 129.1 | 38.8 | 23.2\",\"supports\":\"MD throughput proxy: 265.8 ns/day on one A100 for an 80,289-atom protein-in-membrane system.\"},{\"id\":\"s_a100min\",\"url\":\"https://tools.ranomics.com/help/tools/colabfold\",\"quote\":\"Paste a FASTA (monomer or multimer up to 600 aa total) and get pLDDT, PAE, and pTM/ipTM. ~1 to 2 min on A100-40GB.\",\"supports\":\"Runtime proxy for one AlphaFold job on an A100 40GB.\"}],\"files_read\":[\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11381518\",\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12682079\",\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10115422\",\"https://lambda.ai/pricing\",\"https://www.voyagertherapeutics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/POSTER-Voyager_ASGCT_2024_FINAL_Ishan.pdf (fetched; PDF text not extractable in this session, so no claim rests on unverified poster text)\",\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6855452\",\"https://journals.plos.org/plosbiology/article?id=10.1371%2Fjournal.pbio.3002112\",\"https://www.voyagertherapeutics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/POSTER-Voyager_ASGCT_Spring_2024_03_Hoffman_FRIDAY_4-26.pdf\",\"https://ir.voyagertherapeutics.com/news-releases/news-release-details/voyager-therapeutics-presents-data-second-generation-tracertm\",\"https://www.voyagertherapeutics.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/BioCentury_Voyagers-journey-to-identify-a-new-shuttle-for-bringing-gene-therapies-into-the-brain.pdf\",\"https://hpc.fau.de/2024/08/13/gromacs-2024-1-on-brand-new-gpgpus/\",\"https://tools.ranomics.com/help/tools/colabfold\",\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9184281\",\"producer.md (written this session)\",\"pilot/run_pilot.py (written this session; executed later by phase p1_pilot on the Lambda instance)\"]}","time":{"start":1792549180434,"end":1792549297794}}}
